                Blocks(
                    Paragraph(Text("Let theta be a finite original stationary binary edge presentation and J a probability measure with exactly theta's original marked integer-time cylinders. Let D be an actual closed communicating class of the support of M_0+M_1, with positive original stationary mass c, and let kappa be nativeComponent(theta,D,c-positive). Fix a nonempty Boolean word w and a rectangle R for product(kappa,w), with r in its row support. The hidden type in the conclusion is exactly the subtype D; kappa keeps the original matrix entries, normalizes the original stationary masses by c, and retains the scalar stationary no11 condition. No irreducibility, periodicity, unifilarity, positive global matrix, or extra posterior hypothesis is supplied.")),
                    Paragraph(Text("The theorem first supplies the bounded positive labelled route family a from every h in D to r by applying irreducible_rectangle_occurrence to the actual closed-class restriction. It retains the empty route at r, the length bound card(D), the first-one final-zero seam, structural zeros, and the exact selectedEpsilon(kappa,w,r,a). The block length is b=length(w)+card(D); rho=1-u/v uses the minimum and maximum of the actual rectangle entries, and eta=1-epsilon*(1-rho^2).")),
                    Paragraph(Text("For every integer cut t, component_restriction identifies c times the inclusion pushforward of K=jointLaw(kappa) with J restricted to state(t) in D. The output coordinate is unchanged by inclusion. The same law's visible pushforward K.map Prod.snd is identified with the existing visibleLaw(kappa) used by OriginalErasureComparison.leftRisk and rightRisk, so no convenient redefined risk or unrelated posterior law is introduced.")),
                    Paragraph(Text("For every j>=0, the finite posterior ratio is the existing bitPredictor conditional expectation on the exact finite record, including null observation fibers; the ordered limits retain the entire opposite infinite half-line. The left and right pointwise defects are bounded under the same class law K=jointLaw(kappa) by rho raised to the chronological original b-block counts starting at -floor(j/b)*b and 1. Squaring and the chronological occurrence moment give leftRisk(kappa,j), rightRisk(kappa,j) <= eta^(floor(j/b)). The statement preserves j=0, rho=0, eta=0, and the natural 0^0=1 convention without division by rho or eta.")),
                    Paragraph(Text("The public tail conclusion defines rootErasureTail(kappa,R) as the sum over j>=R of the square roots of the two existing risks and keeps erasureTail(kappa,R) as the existing sum of the two risks in extended reals. Existing OriginalUnifilarErasureTail.tail_series is consumed with rho=sqrt(eta) for the root tail and eta for the squared tail, yielding rootErasureTail(kappa,R) <= 2*b*(sqrt(eta))^(floor(R/b))/(1-sqrt(eta)), erasureTail(kappa,R) <= 2*b*eta^(floor(R/b))/(1-eta), and rootErasureTail(kappa,0) <= 2*b/(1-sqrt(eta)). The endpoint and zero-rate cases remain in the same statement."))),
